# Line endings are LF in the index and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf on Windows checks files out as CRLF while the
# tools here write LF, and git reports every touched file as modified with an
# empty diff. That is not only noise: `git status --porcelain -- acceptance/`
# is what this repository uses to prove an acceptance test was not reshaped to
# make an implementation pass, and it reported all nine of them as changed when
# none had been. A check that cries wolf is a check nobody reads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated. Keep it out of diffs and out of language statistics.
bun.lock linguist-generated=true
